<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajaraja I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 985–<a href="/years/1014">1014</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Rajaraja Chola I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajaraja I was emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, reigning from 985 to 1014. He conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> and Chera lands, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, where he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anuradhapura">Anuradhapura</a> in 993, and the Maldives, and he ended Western Ganga rule at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talakad">Talakad</a>. He built the Brihadishvara temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> and organised a strong navy and a survey of land revenue.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaraja-i.jpg" alt="Rajaraja I" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Venu62 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raraja_detail.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
